  "prefLabel": "Plc 1607.03 Rehearings and Appeals",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Plc 1607.03 Rehearings and Appeals.\n\n(a) As provided in RSA 310:14, I:\n\n(1) Any person who has been denied a registration under this chapter shall have the right to a rehearing; and\n\n(2) Requests for a rehearing shall be made within 30 days of receipt of the original final decision.\n\n(b) Pursuant to RSA 310:14, II, any person who has been disciplined shall have the right to petition in writing for a rehearing within 30 days of receipt of the original final decision.\n\n(c) Petitions or requests for rehearing shall be made in the form of a motion as provided in Plc 206.12.\n\n(d) Pursuant to RSA 310:14, III:\n\n(1) Appeals from a decision on rehearing shall be by appeal to the supreme court pursuant to RSA 541; and\n\n(2) No sanction shall be stayed during an appeal.\n\nSource. #13914, eff 5-6-24\n\nAppendix A: State Statutes Implemented",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/plc1600.html"
